  "narrative": {
    "top_frame": "Texas buried this game in the third inning, and the Giants never found an answer.",
    "what_this_means": "Eight runners left on base across six missed-opportunity innings tells the whole story. Whisenhunt lasted 3.1 innings and gave up four runs before the bullpen. Seymour, Foley, Beck combining for 4.2 scoreless frames. Arrived too late to matter. The lineup produced eight hits and ten strikeouts, a mute combination that said nothing when it needed to say everything. Shut out 6-0 at Globe Life Field is not a loss you recover from in a season like this one. It's confirmation of what keeps happening: the Giants keep leaving runners on base in the exact innings when they need to convert them, and the margin between staying close and falling apart is thinner than they can afford.",
